AID TOKEN DEFINITIONS-TESTS
ATITLE CDATA Definition Tests
(SUITE
AID TOKEN DEFINITIONS
ATITLE CDATA Definitions
(CATEGORY
(PROSE
-Definitions declare new types that can be used throughout a program.\n\n    
)PROSE
AID TOKEN STRUCTURE-DEFINITIONS
ATITLE CDATA Structure Definitions
(TESTS
(PROSE
-The define keyword creates a new structure type with named properties.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN DEFINE-POINT
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Point(x: int, y: int)\nPoint(3, 4)
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-{"_type":"Point","x":3,"y":4}\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN DEFINE-FIELD-ACCESS
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Point(x: int, y: int)\nPoint(3, 4).x
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-3\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN DEFINE-WITH-LET
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Point(x: int, y: int)\nlet p Point(3, 4)\np.x + p.y
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-7\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN DEFINE-NESTED
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Point(x: int, y: int)\ndefine Rectangle(origin: Point, width: int, height: int)\nRectangle(Point(0, 0), 10, 5).width
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-10\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN UNION-DEFINITIONS
ATITLE CDATA Union Definitions
(TESTS
(PROSE
-Unions define types with multiple variants. Each variant can optionally carry a value.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN OPTION-SOME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option union(Some: int, None)\nSome(5)
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-{"_type":"Option","_variant":"Some","value":5}\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN OPTION-NONE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option union(Some: int, None)\nNone
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-{"_type":"Option","_variant":"None"}\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN RESULT-OK
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union(Ok: int, Err: String)\nOk(42)
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-{"_type":"Result","_variant":"Ok","value":42}\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN RESULT-ERR
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Result union(Ok: int, Err: String)\nErr("error")
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-{"_type":"Result","_variant":"Err","value":"error"}\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN OPTION-SOME-VALUE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-define Option union(Some: int, None)\nOption.Some(5).value
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-5\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN FUNCTION-NAMES
ATITLE CDATA Function Names
(TESTS
(PROSE
-A routine's role is set by its declaration keyword, not by how its\n        name is spelled. A function may be named with ordinary letters, with a\n        single-quoted string identifier (which may contain spaces), or with\n        operator characters; in every case it is an ordinary function, applied\n        by writing its name before a parenthesized argument.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN FUNCTION-QUOTED-NAME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-function 'add seven'(n: int) returns int\n    n + 7\n'add seven'(35)
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN FUNCTION-OPERATOR-CHAR-NAME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-function ++(n: int) returns int\n    n + 1\n++(41)
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n\n    
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
AID TOKEN OPERATOR-DEFINITIONS
ATITLE CDATA Operator Definitions
(TESTS
(PROSE
-The operator keyword declares an operator, applied infix between\n        its two operands. Like functions, operators may be named with operator\n        characters or with a text or single-quoted name. Operators may be\n        declared at the top level, not only inside a type. A text-named operator\n        binds more weakly than the built-in arithmetic operators, so the\n        arithmetic combines first.\n        
)PROSE
AID TOKEN OPERATOR-SYMBOLIC
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-operator <+>(left: int, right: int) returns int\n    left + right\n40 <+> 2
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN OPERATOR-TEXT-NAME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-operator 'plus'(left: int, right: int) returns int\n    left + right\n40 'plus' 2
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN OPERATOR-QUOTED-NAME
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-operator 'divided by'(left: int, right: int) returns int\n    left / right\n84 'divided by' 2
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-42\n        
)EXPECT
)TEST
AID TOKEN OPERATOR-PRECEDENCE
ASKIP IMPLIED
APROGRAM TOKEN PROGRAM
(TEST
(INPUT
-operator 'minus'(left: int, right: int) returns int\n    left - right\n20 'minus' 3 + 5
)INPUT
(EXPECT
-12\n
)EXPECT
)TEST
)TESTS
)CATEGORY
)SUITE
C
